My professional background is firmly rooted in publishing management, and my expertise is in metadata analysis, QA, and open-access publication. I face a very specific hurdle in today's job market. As I actively apply for full-time roles in academic libraries, I constantly see that employers strictly require formal research data management (RDM) skills to fulfill their operational requirements. This selected course will perfectly bridge the gap between my current publishing expertise and the modern demands of data librarianship. By learning FAIR data principles and the research data lifecycle, I can translate my metadata skills into the exact RDM competencies hiring managers need. My career goal is to acquire a full-time position in data curation. This certificate will provide the verified credential I need to prove my RDM knowledge, bypass automated resume filters, and secure a stable library job.